---

## 2. Executive Summary
Sam Robinson breaks down his blueprint for earning $12,000/month by offering modernized, mobile-first one-page websites to local blue-collar contractors (roofers, plumbers, electricians, landscapers) who have outdated, broken, or missing websites. Instead of trying to close high-friction phone sales, he builds a fast mockup and sends a personalized 60-second video audit.

---

## 3. The Money Math & Economic Reality
**The Local Business Leverage:**
- Blue-collar trades earn massive ticket sizes per completed job:
  - Roofer: $5,000 – $15,000 per roof replacement
  - Plumber / HVAC: $2,000 – $8,000 per replacement / repair
  - Remodeler: $10,000 – $40,000 per kitchen/bath remodel
- If your website mockup helps them land just **ONE** additional customer, the site pays for itself 5x over.
- **Pricing Models:**
  - $400 – $750 flat setup fee
  - OR $150 – $250/month (including hosting, basic edits, and Google profile updates)
- To make **$3,000/month**, you only need **6 clients at $500 flat**, or **15 monthly retainers at $200/mo**.

---

## 4. Step-by-Step Implementation Blueprint
1. **Step 1: Finding High-Ticket Trades on Google Maps:**
   - Search: `"Roofers in [City Name]"`, `"Plumbing contractors in [City Name]"`, `"Kitchen remodelers in [City Name]"`.
   - Scroll to pages 2, 3, and 4.
   - Look for listings with broken links, missing websites, or sites built 10 years ago that don't load properly on mobile.
2. **Step 2: Rapid 15-Minute Mockup:**
   - Pick a clean, high-converting contractor template on Framer, Carrd, Webflow, or WordPress.
   - Insert their logo, phone number, service areas, customer testimonials (from their Google Maps reviews), and a large click-to-call button.
3. **Step 3: The 60-Second Video Audit (Loom):**
   - Open their current website on your screen and open your redesigned mobile preview side-by-side.
   - Pitch script:
     > *"Hey [Contractor Name], I was searching for local roofers in [City] and noticed your site is hard to read on iPhone and doesn't have a direct click-to-call button, which is likely costing you quote requests every week. I took 15 minutes to mock up a fast mobile version for your business. Here's what it looks like: [demo]. If you want it, I can launch it on your domain this Friday for a flat $350. If not, feel free to keep the design ideas!"*
4. **Step 4: The Follow-Up & Close:**
   - Send 15 of these Loom audits per day via email, Facebook business message, or contact forms.
   - When they agree, send a Stripe payment link and connect their domain.

---

## 5. Required Tools & Software Stack
- **Prospecting:** Google Maps & Google Business Profiles (Free)
- **Video Screen Recording:** Loom (Free up to 25 videos)
- **Website Builder:** Carrd ($19/year) or Framer / Webflow (Free tiers)
- **Payments:** Stripe / PayPal (Free setup)

---

## 6. Beginner ("Noob") Reality Check
| Metric | Assessment |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Upfront Capital Needed** | **$0** |
| **Technical Difficulty** | **3 / 10** (Using templates, zero code) |
| **Time to First Dollar** | **3 – 7 Days** (Highest certainty) |

### Critical Pitfalls & Hidden Traps:
- Don't try to build a 20-page complex corporate website. Blue-collar contractors only care about 3 things: phone number, services offered, and customer trust proof.
- Don't get discouraged by non-responses; send 15–20 pitches daily for 5 business days to guarantee your first deal.

---

## 7. Action Plan for a Complete Beginner
```markdown
Day 1: Set up a free Loom account and bookmark 1 clean roofer template on Carrd/Framer.
Day 2: Identify 25 roofers and plumbers on Google Maps with poor websites.
Day 3: Record and send 15 personalized 60-second video audits.
Day 4: Send 15 more video audits and follow up on opened emails.
Day 5: Close your first client for $350-$500 and deliver within 24 hours.
```

